%I A011958 #27 Aug 06 2026 07:54:36
%S A011958 1,1,3,8,22,68,216,728,2513,8920,32116,117240,431550,1600734,5970704,
%T A011958 22381184,84236890,318191804,1205692236,4581481776,17452915218,
%U A011958 66637798834,254960616136,977346581800,3753005281872,14434625803920,55600017771599,214457171447220
%N A011958 Number of CdI_2 polytypes that repeat after 2n layers.
%C A011958 The values in McLarnan's Table 5 are correct, but the expression given for I'(N) on p. 280 cannot be implemented as printed. Its second summand should be 2*N*(2^N - (-1)^N)/3 = 2*N*A001045(N), so the cosine argument should be (N-1)*Pi rather than (N-1)*Pi/3. The first summand, Sum_{d|N} phi(d)*T(N,d), is correct as printed. Using the printed expression directly gives half-integer values for N congruent to 2 and 0 mod 3, as noted by _R. J. Mathar_. With that one correction the formulas of the paper reproduce this sequence. - _Daniel Okwor_, Aug 05 2026
%H A011958 Daniel Okwor, <a href="/A011958/b011958.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..300</a>
%H A011958 T. J. McLarnan, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1524/zkri.1981.155.3-4.269">The numbers of polytypes in close-packings and related structures</a>, Zeits. Krist. 155, 269-291 (1981).
%F A011958 a(n) = Sum_{d|n} mu(n/d)*(Ip(d) + Ipp(d))/2, where Ip(N) = (Sum_{d|N} phi(d)*T(N,d) + 2*N*(2^N - (-1)^N)/3)/(2*N) with T(N,d) = 2^(2*N/d) if 3 divides d and (2^(2*N/d) + 2)/3 otherwise, and Ipp(N) = (Sum_{d|N/2} phi(2*d)*2^(N/d))/(2*N) for even N and 0 for odd N. - _Daniel Okwor_, Aug 05 2026
%o A011958 (PARI) T(N,d) = my(m=2*N/d); if(d%3==0, 2^m, (2^m+2)/3);
%o A011958 Ip(N) = (sumdiv(N, d, eulerphi(d)*T(N,d)) + 2*N*(2^N-(-1)^N)/3)/(2*N);
%o A011958 Ipp(N) = if(N%2, 0, sumdiv(N/2, d, eulerphi(2*d)*2^(N/d))/(2*N));
%o A011958 a(n) = sumdiv(n, d, moebius(n/d)*(Ip(d)+Ipp(d))/2); \\ _Daniel Okwor_, Aug 05 2026
%Y A011958 Cf. A001045, A011768, A011947, A011957.
%K A011958 nonn,easy
%O A011958 1,3
%A A011958 _N. J. A. Sloane_
%E A011958 a(26)-a(28) from _Daniel Okwor_, Aug 05 2026
